    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ălētrĭum</span></b> ,
		i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Latium</i>, now <i>Alatri;</i> whence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ălētrīnas</span></b> ,
				ātis, adj., <i>pertaining to Aletrium</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Clu. 16</span></i>. —<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ălētrīnātes</span></b> ,
				<i>the inhabitants of Aletrium</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Clu. 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, §
			63</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			Also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ălētrīnensis</span></b> ,
			e, the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">foederatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Balb. 22</span></i>
			 dub.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
